Subject: [PATCH] chrome: compose the profile early in browser startup

The browser composes its profile at the end of the user-data-dir step in
ChromeMainDelegate::PreSandboxStartup, before the zygote fork and before
any child process exists. Every child command line then carries the
profile switch. On Linux, a later composition would miss the zygote, and
every renderer forked from it would report host values such as
navigator.hardwareConcurrency. The fixed point also keeps the browser
and its renderers in agreement, for example the Device-Memory header and
navigator.deviceMemory. Nothing is written to disk.

--- a/chrome/app/chrome_main_delegate.cc
+++ b/chrome/app/chrome_main_delegate.cc
@@ -9,6 +9,7 @@
 #include <string>
 #include <variant>
 
+#include "base/apostate/compose.h"
 #include "base/base_paths.h"
 #include "base/check.h"
 #include "base/command_line.h"
@@ -1376,6 +1377,39 @@
     InitializeUserDataDir(base::CommandLine::ForCurrentProcess());
   }
 
+  // Apostate: decide this launch's device profile here, in the browser, and
+  // put it on the command line before anything can copy that command line.
+  //
+  // The compositor used to run lazily, from the profile loader's first use.
+  // That made the identity a function of whichever subsystem happened to ask
+  // for a profile field first, which is not a decision anyone made. Two
+  // consequences were real rather than theoretical. On Linux, content forks
+  // the zygote from ContentMainRunnerImpl::Initialize, after this function and
+  // before PostEarlyInitialization; the zygote's command line is built by
+  // AppendExtraCommandLineSwitches, so a profile installed later than this
+  // never reaches it, and the zygote caching a null profile before forking
+  // hands every renderer the host's values. And on every platform the browser
+  // sizes pools from SysInfo, which consults the profile, so a profile
+  // installed after that point makes the browser and the renderer disagree
+  // about the same machine.
+  //
+  // This is the earliest point that satisfies both conditions the compositor
+  // needs. InitializeUserDataDir just ran, so chrome::DIR_USER_DATA is
+  // resolved -- which the command-line switch alone does not give us, because
+  // on POSIX that switch is appended back only when the requested directory
+  // was invalid. And no child process of any type exists yet: content calls
+  // PreSandboxStartup before SandboxInitialized, before the zygote fork, and
+  // long before BrowserMainLoop. BasicStartupComplete is earlier still, but
+  // the user data directory is not resolved there.
+  //
+  // Only the browser composes. A child carries --type and receives the
+  // profile it was given.
+  if (process_type.empty()) {
+    base::FilePath user_data_dir;
+    base::PathService::Get(chrome::DIR_USER_DATA, &user_data_dir);
+    base::apostate::InstallComposedProfile(user_data_dir);
+  }
+
   // Register component_updater PathProvider after DIR_USER_DATA overridden by
   // command line flags. Maybe move the chrome PathProvider down here also?
   component_updater::RegisterPathProvider(chrome::DIR_COMPONENTS,
